<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ngo Xuong Ngap</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 954</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Ngô Xương Ngập</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ngo Xuong Ngap was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-quyen">Ngo Quyen</a>, founder of the Ngo dynasty in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duong-tam-kha">Duong Tam Kha</a> usurped the throne in 944 he went into hiding, and after his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ngo-xuong-van">Ngo Xuong Van</a> overthrew the usurper in 950 the two ruled jointly, Ngap with the title Thien Sach Vuong. His death in 954 left Xuong Van as sole ruler.</p></div>
